## 1. Install pnpm

If you already have Node.js installed:

```bash
npm install -g pnpm
```

Verify:

```bash
node -v
pnpm -v
```

For modern Node.js, Corepack is another good option:

```bash
corepack enable
corepack prepare pnpm@latest --activate
```

---

## 2. Create the project

```bash
mkdir ecommerce
cd ecommerce

pnpm init
```

Create:

```text
apps/
packages/
```

On Windows:

```powershell
mkdir apps
mkdir packages
```

---

## 3. Create `pnpm-workspace.yaml`

At the root:

```yaml
packages:
  - "apps/*"
  - "packages/*"
```

This tells pnpm:

> Treat every directory under `apps` and `packages` as a workspace package.

